{"task_id": "Mbpp/57", "solution": "from typing import List\nclass Validator:\n    \"\"\"\n    Validation component enforcing each element is a single digit 0..9.\n    Raises ValueError on invalid input.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.allowed_min = 0\n        self.allowed_max = 9\n\n    def validate(self, digits: List[int]) -> None:\n        if not isinstance(digits, list):\n            raise ValueError(\"Input must be a list of digits\")\n        for v in digits:\n            if not _is_single_digit(v):\n                raise ValueError(f\"Invalid digit: {v}\")\ndef _is_single_digit(value: object) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a value is an integer digit between 0 and 9 inclusive.\"\"\"\n    return isinstance(value, int) and 0 <= value <= 9\ndef find_Max_Num(digits: List[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the largest number that can be formed with the given list of digits.\n    Validates input, sorts digits descending, concatenates, returns integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    Validator().validate(digits)\n    if len(digits) == 0:\n        return 0\n    sorted_digits = sorted(digits, reverse=True)\n    numeric_string = ''.join(str(d) for d in sorted_digits)\n    return int(numeric_string)"}
