{"task_id": "Mbpp/475", "solution": "import functools\nclass SortCounter:\n    \"\"\"\n    Encapsulates the logic for sorting dictionary items and input validation.\n    This class is designed to be stateless.\n    \"\"\"\n    def validate_input(self, obj):\n        \"\"\"\n        Checks if the provided object is a dictionary.\n        Raises TypeError if the input is not a dictionary.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(obj, dict):\n            raise TypeError(\"input must be a dict\")\n\n    def compare_entries(self, entry_a, entry_b):\n        \"\"\"\n        Compares two (key, value) tuples.\n        Orders by value descending, then key ascending.\n        \"\"\"\n        key_a, value_a = entry_a\n        key_b, value_b = entry_b\n\n        # Primary sort: value descending\n        if value_a > value_b:\n            return -1\n        elif value_a < value_b:\n            return 1\n        else:\n            # Secondary sort: key ascending (tie-break)\n            if key_a < key_b:\n                return -1\n            elif key_a > key_b:\n                return 1\n            else:\n                return 0\n\n    def sort_counter(self, input_dict):\n        \"\"\"\n        Validates, sorts, and returns dictionary items as a list of tuples.\n        Catches comparison TypeErrors and re-raises as ValueError.\n        \"\"\"\n        self.validate_input(input_dict)\n        items = list(input_dict.items()) # Create a new list to avoid modifying the original\n\n        try:\n            # Use functools.cmp_to_key to adapt the custom comparison function\n            sorted_items = sorted(items, key=functools.cmp_to_key(self.compare_entries))\n            return sorted_items\n        except TypeError as e:\n            # Catch TypeErrors that can occur during comparison of non-comparable types\n            raise ValueError(\"values not comparable\") from e\ndef sort_counter(input_dict):\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a dictionary by its values in descending order.\n    Uses keys in ascending order as a tie-breaker for equal values.\n    \"\"\"\n    return SortCounter().sort_counter(input_dict)"}
