{"task_id": "Mbpp/586", "solution": "def _compute_rotation(input_list, n_mod_len):\n    \"\"\"\n    Performs the list rotation using slicing.\n    \"\"\"\n    return input_list[n_mod_len:] + input_list[:n_mod_len]\ndef split_Arr(input_list, n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Splits a list at the nth element and moves the first part to the end.\n    Performs a left-rotation of the list by n positions.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_list:\n        return []\n\n    # Calculate the effective rotation index using the modulo operator.\n    # This correctly handles n greater than list length, n equal to 0,\n    # and implicitly handles negative n as a right shift.\n    n_mod_len = n % len(input_list)\n    \n    return _compute_rotation(input_list, n_mod_len)"}
